# 02 — Migrate MLDPWriter to BaseQueuedWriter

**Depends on**: `01-base-queued-writer` complete.

## Goal

Replace all queue/backpressure/thread-pool boilerplate in `MLDPWriter` with the
`BaseQueuedWriter<QueueItem>` base class.  No behavior change — existing log
lines, metrics, stream lifecycle, and gRPC send path are untouched.

---

## Checklist

### Header (`include/writer/mldp/MLDPWriter.h`)

- [ ] Change base: `IWriter` → `BaseQueuedWriter<QueueItem>`
- [ ] Remove private members now owned by base:
  - `channels_`
  - `queuedItems_`
  - `backpressureMutex_`, `backpressureCv_`
  - `threadPool_`
  - `nextChannel_`
  - inner struct `WorkerChannel`
- [ ] Keep private: `ingestionPool_`, `providerId_`, `StreamState`, `lastEventTime_`,
  `lastEventTimeMutex_`, `pushLogMutex_`, `lastPushLogTime_`
- [ ] Add `override` on `toItems()` and `processItem()`
- [ ] Remove `start()`, `stop()`, `forceStop()` declarations (base owns them)
- [ ] Keep `isHealthy()`, `acceptsPayload()`, `providerId()`

### Source (`src/writer/mldp/MLDPWriter.cpp`)

- [ ] Delete `start()` implementation (thread pool + channel init) — replace with
  `doStart()`: provider registration + `ingestionPool_` init + `workerCount()`
  sized `lastEventTime_` pre-reserve if desired.
- [ ] Delete `stop()` implementation — replace with `doStop()`:
  `ingestionPool_.reset()`.
- [ ] Delete `forceStop()` implementation.
- [ ] Convert `push()`:
  - Keep payload validation (TimeSeries check, end_of_batch_group skip)
  - Keep per-frame loop that builds `QueueItem` per frame
  - Replace blocking-push + `channels_[idx]` enqueue with:
    `return BaseQueuedWriter::push(std::move(batch));`
    OR implement `toItems()` directly (preferred — see below).
- [ ] Implement `toItems(batch)`:
  - Validates payload type, skips `end_of_batch_group`
  - Iterates frames, skips empty timestamps
  - Returns `vector<QueueItem>` — one item per frame
  - Rate-limited push log (`lastPushLogTime_`) moves here
- [ ] Implement `processItem(workerIdx, item)`:
  - Body = existing `workerLoop` minus dequeue/shutdown/drain logic
  - `ensureStream`, stream age/bytes check, `buildRequest`, `Write`, metrics
  - Call `notifySlotFree()` is automatic (base calls it after `processItem` returns)
- [ ] `workerLoop()` private method removed entirely.
- [ ] `updateQueueDepthMetric()` — base calls `notifySlotFree()` which can be
  hooked; OR keep as explicit call at end of `processItem()`.

### Rate-limited push log placement

Current log (every 10s): `"Pushed N element(s) for source '{}', queue depth: {}"`.
Move into `toItems()` since that is the push hot path.  Use `queueDepth()` helper
from base for the depth value.

